MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_001: Hm, I need to pack light, but it's so hard to figure out\nwhat to keep and what to toss...
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_002: I need this. I don't need this. Oh yeah, this thing...
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_003: Alright, Sha Lan, tossed those broken bottles for ya.\nWhat now?
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_004: Ah, thank you, Nezha. Can you sort through this bag\nfor me?
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_005: "Sort"? Why not just keep everything in there?
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_006: Don't be silly. You have to properly separate what\nyou need from what you don't.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_007: What a pain... I shouldn't have agreed to help.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_008: What was that?
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_009: Oh, nothing. I'll just try to hustle through this.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_010: Hrm, these bandages are still good. And this thing\nhere is... Huh?
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_011: What a pretty little box. What's in here? Ahhh!
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_012: What's wrong?!
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_013: So it's been in this bag all along! No wonder I\ncouldn't find it...
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_014: Who cares! Why do you have it?
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_015: The stone in here—isn't this the one I was holding\nwhen I was born?
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_016: Yes, that's right. The little lump of nutrients that\nwould normally form bones.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_017: I think it leaked out due to a manufacturing defect\nand became a stone.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_018: Ugh, damn, that's right. That's the reason I didn't\ngrow taller!
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_019: If things had worked out how they were supposed to,\nI would've been born with an adult body.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_020: You were born as an adult, just a little shorter.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_021: Shut up! And answer my question. Why do you\nhave it?
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_022: Because it's important. You gave it to me. Don't you\nremember?
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_023: I did? Oh, wait, yeah!
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_024: Yeah, you recall. Now then, if you're satisfied, hand\nit over.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_025: Hey, stop! Don't take it! I wanna throw it away!
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_026: Too bad. If you want it, come and get it.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_027: Nooooo! Knock it off! You're way too tall—I\ncan't reach!
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_028: What do you mean "way too tall"? Rude. Anyway,\nit's mine.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_029: You're doing this to mess with me! If you don't toss\nthat trash, I'll get angry.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_030: You're angry already, aren't you? Alright, alright, I'll\nthrow it away for you.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_C_031: You better!
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_001: Sha Laaaan...
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_002: What is it? You sound annoyed.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_003: Of course I'm annoyed! You still have that\nstupid rock!
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_004: Anatolia said she saw it. You told me you were\ngonna throw it away, you liar!
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_005: Oh, she did? Well, I wasn't lying.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_006: I didn't specify that I'd throw the stone itself away.\nI did throw away that box though.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_007: That's a buncha crap! Gimme the stone, you jerk!
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_008: No, I will most certainly not. It's my treasure.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_009: When you gave it to me...that's when we became\nfamily.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_010: Huh? What are you talking about? We've always\nbeen family.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_011: Your mom was a nurse to me and Anatolia. She told\nme to think of you as my sister.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_012: That's right. I was supposed to help my mother to\neducate you.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_013: I was so nervous. It felt like a big job to care for the\nMediator meant to save the whole village.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_014: You were both so innocent when you were new to\nthe world. You watched my every move closely.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_015: I felt worried because I thought my behavior would\ninfluence you, for better or for worse.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_016: I... I was so nervous...
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_017: Oh...
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_018: I was only ever assisting my mother, but I needed to\nput on a confident face.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_019: I remember peptalking myself in front of the mirror,\nand then you were there behind me...
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_020: You handed me this stone. It made me so happy... It\nfelt like you were quietly encouraging me.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_021: That's not what I was trying to do.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_022: Oh, so you just gave it to me because you didn't need\nit? That's OK too... I was thinking selfishly...
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_023: No, no, it's not like that either! I... I just...
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_024: What is it?
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_025: I...
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_026: I get it now. It's important to you. So you don't have\nto throw it away.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_027: Just don't let anyone see it, OK? See ya.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_B_028: Wait, don't go! Nezha!
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_001: Hey. I want you to tell me.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_002: You're so annoying—can't you let it go? Who cares\nwhy I gave you a dumb rock.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_003: I care. It's my treasure. Please tell me why, Nezha.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_004: Oh, come on. Don't make that face...
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_005: I just wanted to get your attention. That's all.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_006: What do you mean?
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_007: Your mom called Anatolia "Rui Ji."
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_008: The name of her dead daughter... The name of\nyour sister.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_009: I remember she accidentally called her that once, and\nthen the nickname kinda stuck.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_010: Yeah... I started calling her Rui Ji after that too.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_011: I felt lonely. I didn't have anything like that...
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_012: But, that's—
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_013: It's not like I was treated differently or anything.\nI just didn't look like Rui Ji.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_014: But I was still so new...so I didn't understand, and my\nfeelings were hard to express...
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_015: I had nothing—just some dumb rock I was holding\nbecause of the malfunction...
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_016: So because you didn't have the words, you gave\nit to me.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_017: Now that I think about it, it feels embarrassing that I\nwas hurt just because I didn't have a nickname.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_018: But you and your mom really cared about me...
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_019: Of course!
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_020: Whoa! What's with the hug...
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_021: I'm sorry... I'm so sorry. I never knew you felt\nthat way.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_022: Instead, I thought it was you trying to make me\nfeel better...
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_023: Don't cry! I didn't know you were feeling bad, either.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_024: I mean, I didn't even remember giving you the stone.\nLet's just put it to bed, yeah?
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_025: It's not so bad thinking of you like a big sister.\nSomeone I can look after.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_026: Heh... That's silly.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_027: Aw, come on. I'm not just someone you take care of\nanymore. We're equals, aren't we?
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_028: We are. We're both Protectors of Anatolia.
MID_SE_Naz_Sar_A_029: So let's continue to work together. For the sake of our\nprecious family.